    s__GLASS_EYE_CLEAN(py_str("Take it out and clean it: wash the prosthesis in warm water with a little mild soap, rinse it well in saline, and clean the socket with saline on a clean pad, then leave both to air before putting it back. Soreness is usually dryness or a crust that has built up, so a lubricating drop made for prosthesis wearers helps; leave it out overnight if your service says to. Never put the bathroom or contact-lens solutions in it."));
    s__GLASS_EYE_CLINIC(py_str("Ring the prosthetics service or an eye clinic today rather than cleaning it again: a socket that is red, swollen, hot or leaking discharge is an infection or a fit that has changed, and neither is something a clean and a night out fixes. While you wait, take the eye out and rinse it and the socket with saline on a clean pad, keep it out while it is uncomfortable, and never put the bathroom or contact-lens solutions in it. A socket that is badly swollen, or one with spreading redness or a fever, is 111."));
    s__PROSTHESIS_CLEAN(py_str("Wash the socket and the liner every day: mild soap and warm water, rinse both well, and dry them completely before you put them back on - a damp liner is what grows the smell and the sore patches. Turn the liner inside out to wash it if your service says it can be, and leave the leg off at night if that is what your fitter told you. No alcohol, no hot wash and no bathroom cleaners: they harden the liner and the fit goes with it. A liner that has gone tacky, stiff or baggy is worn out rather than dirty, and the limb-fitting service replaces it."));
    s__PROSTHESIS_SORE(py_str("Soreness under a prosthesis is usually the liner or the fit rather than the limb: take it off, wash and dry the liner and the socket, and look at the skin - a red patch that has not faded half an hour after it comes off is the one to show someone. If it rubs where it did not before, ring the limb-fitting service; padding it yourself usually makes the fit worse. A red, hot, swollen or weeping stump is the same week, not the next appointment."));
    s__PROSTHESIS_GIVES_WAY(py_str("A leg that gives way, locks or buckles is an alignment or suspension problem rather than wear: book the limb-fitting service and tell them exactly when it happens - going down stairs, turning, or at the end of the day when the limb has shrunk - because that is what tells them which it is. Use the stick or the crutches you were given until it is looked at, and get it checked the same day if you have fallen on it, or the knee will not straighten and the skin is broken."));
