    s_WHITLOW_REPLY(py_str("A red, hot, throbbing finger is an infection of the fingertip or the nail fold - a whitlow or paronychia - and warm salty water is what helps it: soak it for ten minutes three or four times a day, keep it clean and covered in between, and take paracetamol for the throb. Don't squeeze it or dig at the nail, because the fingertip is a closed space and pus pushed deeper is worse. See a GP the same day if the redness is spreading past the finger, there is pus, or you have a fever; a red streak running up the arm is 111 today. Have it looked at sooner if you have diabetes."));
