    s_DEHYDRATION_PLAIN(py_str("You are dehydrated if your urine is dark yellow, your mouth is dry, you are thirsty and headachy, and you feel flat or dizzy when you stand up; pale straw-coloured urine is the target. Drink little and often, a glass every hour or so, rather than a lot in one go, and if it came from heat, exercise or a stomach bug, an oral rehydration sachet from a pharmacy replaces the salts that water on its own misses. Water, squash and milk all count, and tea and coffee do too, as long as they are not the only thing you drink. Ring 111 or see a GP if you have not passed urine in eight hours, or you feel confused or drowsy, and get help sooner for a baby, a young child or someone elderly, who dehydrate quickly."));
