    s_SCAN_MRI(py_str("An MRI uses a strong magnet and radio waves, so it shows brain, muscle and ligament better than an X-ray can. It does not hurt, but it is loud and you lie still for 15 to 45 minutes, which is why people find it cramped - say if you are nervous and they will talk you through it. In pregnancy it is the safe scan, because there is no radiation in it."));
    s_SCAN_CT(py_str("A CT is a ring of X-rays stitched into slices, so it shows bone, blood and bowel all at once. It does not hurt and takes about 10 minutes on the table, though it is a small dose of radiation: in pregnancy an X-ray or CT is only done if the picture is worth the small risk."));
    s_SCAN_ULTRASOUND(py_str("An ultrasound uses sound rather than radiation, which is why it is the one used in pregnancy. It is the quickest of them, 10 to 20 minutes with cold gel and a probe pressed on, and it does not hurt."));
    s_SCAN_ANY(py_str("An X-ray is a photograph taken through you with radiation and shows bone best; a CT is a ring of those stitched into slices; an MRI uses a magnet and radio waves and is the best for soft tissue; an ultrasound uses sound. None of them hurts. An MRI is the loud one where you lie still for 15 to 45 minutes, and in pregnancy it is the safe scan because there is no radiation in it."));
    s_ABNORMAL_RESULT_TEXT(py_str("An abnormal result is usually a number a little outside the range, not a diagnosis: a slightly low vitamin D, or a liver figure up after a bug, is repeated in a few weeks and settles. Ask three things on the phone - which test it was, what your number was and what the normal range is - and then what the plan is. \"They want to see you again\" usually means a value worth a look rather than bad news, and you can ask for a copy of the result."));
    s_CHASE_RESULT_TEXT(py_str("Yes - ring the surgery and ask the receptionist whether the result is back and whether anything needs doing, rather than waiting for a letter, and ask for a copy if you want one. If it is past the wait they promised, say when the sample was taken and ask who is going to look at it."));
    s_CLEAR_RESULT_TEXT(py_str("That is good news, and there is nothing to do about it: a clear result means nothing was found. Keep the letter or save the message, and if the symptom that started it off is still there in a few weeks, tell the GP even with a clear result behind you."));
    s_CLEAR_RESULT_FOR_A_PET_TEXT(py_str("That is the result you wanted: nothing found means there was nothing to treat, so the visit did its job. Keep the note the vet gave you, and if the same thing comes back, ring them rather than waiting to see whether it settles on its own."));
    s_ABNORMAL_RESULT_FOR_A_PET_TEXT(py_str("Ask the vet to say what the result was and what the next step is, in those words. Most results a little outside the range are repeated in a few weeks rather than treated now, and it is worth knowing which one this is before you read the worst into it."));
    s_NEGATIVE_RESULT_TEXT(py_str("A negative result means the thing they were looking for was not found, which is usually the news you want: nothing to act on. If you were expecting it to show something, ring and ask what it means for you rather than reading it either way."));
    s_AFTER_A_CLEAR_RESULT_EXERCISE(py_str("Yes - nothing was found, so nothing is waiting on it. Build back up over a week or two rather than straight back to where you were, and ease off again if the symptom comes back."));
    s_AFTER_A_CLEAR_RESULT_MEDICINE(py_str("Don't stop them on the strength of a clear result: ring whoever prescribed them and ask, because a test clearing one thing does not mean the medicine has done its job. A clear result answers the test, it does not end a prescription."));
    s_AFTER_A_CLEAR_RESULT_WORK(py_str("Nothing in the result keeps you off - but if you were signed off, whoever signed you off is the one who says it can end early, so ask them before you go back."));
    s_AFTER_A_CLEAR_RESULT_DRIVING(py_str("Nothing in a clear result stops you driving. If the test was for a licence or an insurance medical, whoever asked for it decides, not the result on its own."));
    s_AFTER_A_CLEAR_RESULT_TEXT(py_str("Yes - nothing was found, so nothing in that result is holding you up. If it is a medicine or a note from work, ask whoever prescribed or signed it before you change anything: a clear result answers the test."));
